{"name":"Fairy Kei","title":"Fairy Kei","revision":236303,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Fairy_Kei","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Fairy Kei visuals include:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Conversation hearts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cotton candy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rainbows"},{"kind":"list","text":"Unicorns"},{"kind":"list","text":"Milkshakes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Confetti"},{"kind":"list","text":"Polkadots"},{"kind":"list","text":"Balloons"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vinyl record"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rollerblades"},{"kind":"list","text":"80's & 90's toys"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Fairy Kei is centered around muted pastels and 80's revivalist cartoons and motifs such as My Little Pony G1, Care Bears, Rainbow Brite, vintage 80's Barbie, etc. The look is very much a ‘fantasy style’, emulating the worlds of 80's girls’ cartoons and early shoujo manga. It began with Tavuchi, founder of the vintage and repurposed vintage boutique SPANK!, as her personal style, and then the look took off from there."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Fabric is usually lightweight for dresses and skirts, such as the loose A-line dresses and the fluttery colored petticoats. Thick, fluffy sweaters, over-sized 80's sweatshirts; this is also the land from whence comes the mokomoko accessories craze, and stuffed animals are sewn onto sweaters and scarves, or as the usual purse. Dress length can be ankle length, knee-length or mini-skirt length; anything fluttery and flowy works."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The most important aspects of fairy kei are the vintage/fantasy world factor, and the color palette. Color is one of the most important features here, less so the structure or item. Pastels and neon-tinted pastels, or high-saturated pastels. Popular colors are pastel pink, baby blue, lavender, light yellow and in smaller doses, ‘white-with-black-dots’. Dark and overly bright colors are not allowed outside of accents. Several motifs and themes are often found in fairy kei as well: most notably the unicorn, followed by kittens, any vintage 80's toys or franchises, moons and stars, rainbows, and naturally sweets such as cotton candy and conversation hearts (the chalky American candy that say things like UR CUTE)."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Television"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Anime & Manga"},{"kind":"list","text":"Candy Candy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fairy Princess Minky Momo"},{"kind":"list","text":"Go! Princess PreCure"},{"kind":"list","text":"Little Twin Stars"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Angel Creamy Mami"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Angel Sweet Mint"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Girl Lalabel"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Idol Pastel Yumi"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical Stage Fancy Lala"},{"kind":"list","text":"Marmalade Boy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Persia the Magic Fairy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Princess Sara"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sally the Witch"},{"kind":"list","text":"Secrets of Akko-chan"},{"kind":"list","text":"Star Magician Magical Emi"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Cartoons"},{"kind":"list","text":"80s Barbie series"},{"kind":"list","text":"Care Bears"},{"kind":"list","text":"Herself the Elf"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hello Kitty's Furry Tale Theater"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jem and the Holograms"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lady Lovelylocks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Maxie's World"},{"kind":"list","text":"Moon Dreamers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Muppet Babies"},{"kind":"list","text":"My Little Pony"},{"kind":"list","text":"Popples"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rainbow Brite"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rose Petal Place"},{"kind":"list","text":"Strawberry Shortcake"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Get Along Gang"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wuzzles"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Toys"},{"kind":"list","text":"B.A.B.Y. (Baby Aliens Belonging To You)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Barbie from the 80s & 90s (Happy Birthday 1990, Cool Times Barbie, etc.)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Brush-a-Loves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Care Bears"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cherry Merry Muffin"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cuddle Brites"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cupcake Dolls (90s)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Doodle Bear"},{"kind":"list","text":"Furby"},{"kind":"list","text":"Girl Talk (board game)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Glo Worm"},{"kind":"list","text":"Herself the Elf"},{"kind":"list","text":"Keypers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kitty Check-Up"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kitty Surprise"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lady Lovely Locks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lalaloopsy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Licca-chan"},{"kind":"list","text":"Li'l Miss"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lite-Brite"},{"kind":"list","text":"Little Pretty"},{"kind":"list","text":"Little Twin Stars"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magical girl toys from the 80s (Creamy Mami, Minky Momo, etc.)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magic Bottle Pets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magic Nursery Pets"},{"kind":"list","text":"My Little Pony G1"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nosey Bears"},{"kind":"list","text":"Peppermint Rose"},{"kind":"list","text":"P. J. Sparkles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Polly Pocket G1"},{"kind":"list","text":"Popples"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pound Puppies"},{"kind":"list","text":"Puppy Check-Up"},{"kind":"list","text":"Puppy Surprise"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rainbow Brite"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rose Petal Place"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rub-A-Dub Doggie (Tyco)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shampoodle"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sky Dancers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Snugglebumms"},{"kind":"list","text":"Strawberry Shortacake"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sweet Secrets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sylvanian Families"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tea Bunnies"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tottles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Troll Dolls"},{"kind":"list","text":"Twinkle Bears"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wonder Whims"},{"kind":"list